CC0 1.0 Universal

Statement of Purpose

The laws of most jurisdictions throughout the world automatically confer
exclusive Copyright and Related Rights upon the creator and subsequent
owner(s). The person associating CC0 with a work has chosen to waive those
rights to the fullest extent permitted by law so that the work can be freely
copied, modified, distributed, performed, analysed, mined, and reused for any
purpose, including commercial purposes, without asking permission.

Public-domain dedication

To the greatest extent permitted by, but not in contravention of, applicable
law, Anonymous dedicates to the public domain worldwide all Copyright and
Related Rights held in the original research prose, structured claims,
original diagrams, generated research data, and original public release
records identified as CC0-covered in LICENSES.md.

Fallback licence

If any part of that waiver is judged legally ineffective, the affirmer grants
each affected person a royalty-free, non-transferable, non-sublicensable,
non-exclusive, irrevocable and unconditional licence to exercise those rights
for any purpose, worldwide, for the maximum duration permitted by law.

The work is offered as-is, without warranties, representations, or guarantees
of title, non-infringement, merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose,
accuracy, or absence of defects. Patent and trademark rights are not waived by
CC0. Third-party works are not covered merely because they are cited, described,
or present beside covered material.

